# Fixture-environment cases: run against the small synthetic corpus in
# benchmark/fixtures.py (21 documents + FakeCategoryEmbeddings), not the real
# production index. Fast, deterministic, no network/model download - this is
# what `python -m benchmark run` (no flags) executes by default and what CI
# should run on every PR touching ai_search.py/ui_services.py.
#
# These mirror tests/test_search_relevance.py's 33 (query, expected_document,
# max_rank) cases, adapted to this dataset's schema. Intentional difference:
# tests/test_search_relevance.py pins an exact max rank (tight, fails loudly
# on any regression); this benchmark instead tracks recall/precision/MRR/nDCG
# trends over time at a fixed k=10 - complementary, not a duplicate. Add new
# cases here by copying a line and editing it; no code changes needed.
